        <!-- Overview -->
        <div class="project-section">
            <h2>Overview</h2>

            <p>
                Designed and manufactured a high-power model rocket as part of an 
                L1 rocketry certification project using the Zephyr rocket kit and 
                an H283ST-14A motor. The project involved flight simulation, 
                structural assembly, motor configuration, and preparation for launch. 
            </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Project Workflow -->
        <div class="project-section">
            <h2>Project Workflow</h2>

            <p>
                The rocket was developed through a hands-on engineering process 
                combining flight simulation, fabrication, assembly, and testing. 
                OpenRocket was used to evaluate the expected flight performance and 
                verify the rocket's configuration before launch. 
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>
                    Used OpenRocket to simulate the rocket's flight trajectory, 
                    including expected altitude, velocity, stability, and motor 
                    performance. 
                </li>

                <li>
                    Studied the construction and structural requirements of a 
                    high-power rocket, including airframe, fin, motor mount, and 
                    recovery system components. 
                </li>

                <li>
                    Manufactured and assembled the rocket using the Zephyr rocket 
                    kit, preparing the airframe and components for flight. 
                </li>

                <li>
                    Configured the motor delay using a Universal Delay Drill Tool 
                    (UDDT) based on the simulated flight profile. 
                </li>

                <li>
                    Performed final preparation and launched the completed rocket 
                    as part of the L1 certification attempt. 
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>



